metadata.content:
You've hit a real product boundary, not a gap in your setup. There are two separate distribution systems inside Claude and they don't talk to each other.

Organization settings, Skills and Plugins, pushes to Claude chat, the Desktop chat tab, and Cowork. It does not reach Claude Code. So there's no way to point Claude Code at a brain living inside Claude itself; you found the actual edge.

Claude Code has its own rail: a plugin marketplace, which is just a git repo with a marketplace.json at the root. A plugin can carry skills, subagents, slash commands, hooks, and MCP servers. Your team runs /plugin marketplace add your-org/claude-plugins once and they have the whole stack.

The part that solves your permissions question: move the brain off Google Drive and into a private git repo.

Drive gives you sync. Git gives you what you actually asked for. Branch protection on main means only your named maintainers can merge; everyone else reads, uses, and opens a pull request to suggest a change. You get diff-level review on every prompt edit, full history, and the ability to roll back a skill that started misbehaving last Tuesday. For a distributed team that is the difference between a shared folder and a managed system.

For zero-friction rollout, commit a .claude/settings.json into your working repos:

{
"extraKnownMarketplaces": {
"company-tools": {
"source": { "source": "github", "repo": "your-org/claude-plugins" }
}
},
"enabledPlugins": { "inbox-triage@company-tools": true }
}

When a team member trusts the folder, the marketplace registers and the plugins enable themselves. A new starter is productive without a setup call. Private repos are fine; run gh auth setup-git once and background updates work.

On your two examples specifically, because they are different shapes. Inbox triage and drafting replies is a subagent plus an MCP server for the mail provider, not a skill; skills are instructions, agents are the thing that runs with its own tool access and its own context window. Blog to carousel with brand voice is the classic skill shape: a [SKILL.md](http://SKILL.md) with the procedure, plus a brand-voice reference file sitting next to it, so voice lives in one file that one person owns and everything else reads from.

You will want both rails running. Build the plugin once in git for the Claude Code users, then zip the same skills and upload them under Organization settings, Skills, for the people who live in chat and Cowork. One source of truth, two delivery paths. Check two things before you plan around it: org plugin distribution is Team and Enterprise only, and Cowork plus Skills both need to be enabled. Per-group assignment, so finance sees finance skills and marketing doesn't, is Enterprise.
